1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,900
This shrimp punches so fast, the water

2
00:00:01,900 --> 00:00:03,100
around it briefly boils.

3
00:00:03,620 --> 00:00:04,960
Meet the peacock mantis shrimp.

4
00:00:05,220 --> 00:00:07,030
Small, but it hits with thousands of times

5
00:00:07,030 --> 00:00:07,720
its body weight.

6
00:00:08,080 --> 00:00:10,420
Its club fires at 83 kilometers per hour.

7
00:00:10,860 --> 00:00:12,593
Scientists compare it to a bullet fired

8
00:00:12,593 --> 00:00:13,260
from a handgun.

9
00:00:13,880 --> 00:00:14,800
But here's the weird part.

10
00:00:15,180 --> 00:00:17,177
The strike is so fast, the pressure around

11
00:00:17,177 --> 00:00:17,700
it crashes.

12
00:00:18,220 --> 00:00:19,740
The water turns into vapor bubbles.

13
00:00:20,140 --> 00:00:22,420
Like boiling, but from pressure, not heat.

14
00:00:22,920 --> 00:00:24,200
Then the bubbles collapse...

15
00:00:24,800 --> 00:00:26,240
and hit the target a second time.

16
00:00:26,540 --> 00:00:27,600
One punch, two hits.

17
00:00:28,100 --> 00:00:29,000
But it gets stranger.

18
00:00:29,340 --> 00:00:31,147
The collapsing bubbles give off a tiny

19
00:00:31,147 --> 00:00:31,860
flash of light.

20
00:00:32,460 --> 00:00:33,680
Snail shells crack like eggs.

21
00:00:34,140 --> 00:00:35,652
And the biggest ones can even break

22
00:00:35,652 --> 00:00:36,300
aquarium glass.

23
00:00:36,960 --> 00:00:38,600
So whatever you do...

24
00:00:39,200 --> 00:00:40,300
never tap on its tank.

25
00:00:41,100 --> 00:00:41,700
Subscribe for more.

